 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Ratings and use",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The part is built in a high-cell-density DMOS process for low on-resistance, rugged operation and fast switching, with a high saturation current. It is rated for -0.13 A continuous and -0.52 A pulsed drain current and suits low-voltage circuits that need a low-current high-side switch."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On-resistance is specified at VGS = -5 V. With -2.5 V on the gate the channel saturates near 0.2 A and with -3.0 V near 0.57 A (Figure 1). At VGS = -3.0 V the normalized on-resistance starts at about 1.4 and climbs past 2 by 0.5 A; at -5 V it stays within about 1.12 out to 1 A (Figure 2). Typical gate charge to -5 V is 0.9 nC, with a flat step in VGS near -2.25 V (Figure 7)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "On-resistance rises with junction temperature, from about 0.56 of its 25 °C value at -50 °C to about 1.75 at 150 °C (Figure 3); the table gives 1.9 Ω typical and 17 Ω maximum at 125 °C. The threshold voltage has a typical coefficient of 3 mV/°C. Power dissipation derates by 2.9 mW/°C above 25 °C from 0.36 W."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The source-to-drain body diode is rated for -0.13 A continuous. Its forward drop is -0.8 V typical and -1.2 V maximum at -0.26 A, and falls as temperature rises (Figure 6). Reverse recovery is 10 ns and 3 nC typical at -0.1 A and 100 A/µs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "All thermal figures assume a minimum-pad mounting with RθJA = 350 °C/W. The transient response depends on the circuit board. A single pulse of about 15 ms can dissipate roughly 5 W, falling to about 1 W at 0.3 s and 0.38 W at 100 s (Figure 10)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The top of the package carries the device code SP, a date code M and a Pb-free microdot, which may sit in either of two places; date code orientation and position vary with the factory."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Dimensions and tolerances follow ASME Y14.5M, 2018, in millimetres. The maximum lead thickness includes the lead finish; the minimum is that of the base metal. D and E leave out mold flash, protrusions and gate burrs. The foot length L is taken at a gauge plane 0.25 mm above the seating plane."
  }
 ],
